# Quick IMG Convert — web build context exclusions.
#
# Hard rule (from a real failure on an earlier build): the build
# context must NEVER contain host-installed artifacts. An empty
# .dockerignore once let a 270 MB context including Windows
# node_modules into the image, where COPY . . overwrote the
# Linux-installed dependencies with Windows shims (node.exe: not
# found, exit 127). Every line below is load-bearing.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies INSIDE the image
# (COPY package.json + lockfile -> npm ci -> COPY the remaining
# source), and this file is what keeps host artifacts out of that
# last COPY.

# Host-installed dependencies / build outputs
node_modules
.next
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
# Tests never ship in the production image.
e2e

# Secrets and local state (never in an image)
.env
.env.local
*.db
/data
logs
*.log

# VCS / OS junk
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
